From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:50:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: cfg80211: allow differing max simultaneous links in assoc

cfg80211_mlme_check_mlo_compat() compares the whole MLD Capabilities And
Operations field of the association link and of each other link. The
Maximum Number Of Simultaneous Links subfield of an AP MLD changes when
the AP MLD adds affiliated APs. A Beacon does not replace the elements
of a BSS entry that came from a Probe Response, so entries of one AP MLD
can keep different values. The association then fails with "link MLD
capabilities/ops mismatch".

Ignore that subfield in the compare, like the Recommended Max
Simultaneous Links subfield of the Extended MLD Capabilities. Nothing on
the association path reads it from a BSS entry: mac80211 takes the field
from the Association Response.

Fixes: ccb964b4ab16 ("wifi: cfg80211: validate MLO connections better")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/net/wireless/mlme.c
+++ b/net/wireless/mlme.c
@@ -390,8 +390,14 @@ cfg80211_mlme_check_mlo_compat(const struct ieee80211_multi_link_elem *mle_a,
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
-	if (ieee80211_mle_get_mld_capa_op((const u8 *)mle_a) !=
-	    ieee80211_mle_get_mld_capa_op((const u8 *)mle_b)) {
+	/*
+	 * The Maximum Number Of Simultaneous Links subfield changes when the
+	 * AP adds links, so entries of one AP MLD can hold different values.
+	 */
+	if ((ieee80211_mle_get_mld_capa_op((const u8 *)mle_a) &
+	     ~IEEE80211_MLD_CAP_OP_MAX_SIMUL_LINKS) !=
+	    (ieee80211_mle_get_mld_capa_op((const u8 *)mle_b) &
+	     ~IEEE80211_MLD_CAP_OP_MAX_SIMUL_LINKS)) {
 		NL_SET_ERR_MSG(extack, "link MLD capabilities/ops mismatch");
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
